  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Other Management Consulting Services (NAICS 541618) recorded $160M in obligations for FY2026 to date. The market posted 591 awards with an average award size of $271K, and obligations fell 81.0% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show a peak at $1.3B in FY24, followed by $843M in FY25 and $160M in FY26 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services leads buying with $55M, followed by the Department of Defense with $53.6M and the Department of State with $18.1M. ISLAND PEER REVIEW ORGANIZATION INC topped vendors with $52.4M, followed by PALANTIR USG INC at $27.1M and BATTELLE MEMORIAL INSTITUTE at $14.4M. The buying list also includes the Department of Energy at $12.9M and the Department of Transportation at $5M. The vendor list includes both specialized health contractors and analytics firms, with the top ten vendors ranging from $52.4M down to $4.6M. Contracting activity is concentrated: a few large buyers and vendors account for a sizable share of FY2026 to date obligations, while overall market obligations are materially lower than last fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
